            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ごはん (gohan) is Sino-Japanese (kango): two Chinese characters read with their on'yomi, readings borrowed from Chinese. They are go, \"honourable; a polite prefix\" (Middle Chinese ngjoH) and han, \"cooked rice\" (bjonX) (Unihan, KANJIDIC2; Middle Chinese after Baxter–Sagart). The polite go- is the on'yomi of the character whose native reading gives o-."
            }
          ]
        },
